{"body":"## Source\n\nFound while refreshing CultureMech's vendored MIM label index to `6643131b`. I replayed every recipe label in CultureMech's occurrence table through the old and new pins; the method is from CultureBotAI/CultureMech#417. The pin refresh is a large improvement overall (99% of rows unchanged, and the changes are mostly hydrate-specific corrections). These are the labels where MIM's **current** answer still looks wrong or missing. In each case the old answer was no better, so none of this blocks the pin.\n\n## Wrong form\n\n| CultureMech label | recipe rows | resolves to | problem |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| `MnSO4・xH2O` (+ `MnSO4·nH2O`) | 61 | CHEBI:86364, `MnSO4 x 1 H2O` | A variable hydrate resolves to the monohydrate. The variable-sulfate precedent (#646 and others) gives these a local `x n H2O` identity. |\n| `NiCl2 x H2O`, `NiCl2・H2O` | ~5 | CHEBI:53542, nickel(II) chloride hexahydrate | A monohydrate label resolves to the hexahydrate. |\n| `Trisodium citrate x 3 H2O` | 2 | CHEBI:53258 | A trihydrate label resolves to a non-trihydrate term. |\n| `Potassium phosphate` | 4 | CHEBI:63036 | A generic label resolves to one specific potassium phosphate salt. |\n\nThe NaH2PO4 monohydrate spellings that resolve to the dihydrate record (~36 rows) are already tracked as #758.\n\n## Missing or ambiguous\n\n- **`sodium nitrate`, 58 rows, unresolved:** ambiguous because the stock-solution record `Sodium nitrate (0.70 M stock)` (`kgmicrobe.ingredient:sodium_nitrate_~28070_m_stock~29`) carries the bare compound name as a synonym next to CHEBI:63005. A stock solution's record shouldn't claim the compound's name.\n- **`α-Ketoglutarate`, 3 rows, now unresolved:** #232 correctly retired it from the disodium-salt record as `REJECTED_LABEL`, but no record now claims the anion or acid name.\n- **`Sea Salt`, now unindexed:** the old pin had it ambiguous through two `ontology_label` rows. Either way it got no identity, but no record claims generic sea salt.\n\nThe full replay table is in the CultureMech pin-refresh PR description.\n\n## More from the CultureMech#537 review (same replay)\n\n- **`MgSO4 x H2O` (12 rows) and `MgSO4 . H2O` (1) → CHEBI:31795, magnesium sulfate *heptahydrate*.** These resolve as trusted `mim_exact` through a REJECTED tombstone row on `Mgso47h2o.yaml` that carries the monohydrate label. Under the old pin they were flagged ambiguous; now they're confidently wrong, and KGX emits the edge.\n- **`Na2MoO4.H2O`, `Na2MoO4 . H2O`, `Na2MoO4 · H2O` (3 rows) → CHEBI:75213, the *dihydrate*,** by the same tombstone-row pattern.\n- **`sodium glutarate` (1 row): a regression.** It used to resolve to `cas:13521-83-0` (disodium glutarate). MIM no longer indexes that `ontology_label`, so CultureMech falls back to the recipe's local CHEBI:24329, the glutarate anion: a salt collapsed onto its parent.\n- **NaH2PO4 monohydrate spellings split:** `NaH2PO4•H2O` → CHEBI:114249 (the monohydrate), while `NaH2PO4 x H2O` / `·H2O` go to the dihydrate record (#758). Two spellings of one substance get different identities.\n\nRoot pattern for the first two: merge tombstones keep raw labels naming a *different hydrate* than their survivor, and the label index publishes them as REJECTED rows that consumers follow by contract.\n\n## From the unified-mapping fix (culturebotai-claw#571)\n\n- **`MgSO .7H O` (17 occurrences)** is a safe (`unique`) synonym on the *anhydrous* Magnesium sulfate record (CHEBI:32599), but it's a garbled heptahydrate label. Its recipes carry the correct heptahydrate CHEBI:31795. Now that the unified mapping follows MIM's label index, this MIM synonym placement decides the published identity.\n- **`Na2HPO4·7H2O`** has no label-index row; only other spellings of the heptahydrate are indexed. So its recipes' anhydrous CHEBI:34683 still wins (MIM#808).\n\n## From the claw#571 review: MIM record and synonym defects that now decide unified-mapping identities\n\n| label (occurrences) | MIM's `unique` answer | problem |\n|---|---|---|\n| `DL-Tryptophan` (4) | record `DL-Tryptophan` on CHEBI:57912 | CHEBI:57912 is the L-tryptophan zwitterion, so the racemate is recorded as an enantiomer |\n| `Na2-DL-malate`, `Sodium DL-malate`, `Na-DL-malate` and others (26) | `Sodium malate`, CHEBI:91261 | DL labels sit on a disodium (S)-malate identity |\n| `Na2SiO3` (8) | synonym on `Na2SiO3 x 9 H2O` (CHEBI:132108) | an anhydrous formula label on the nonahydrate |\n| `Magnesium Chloride` (5) | record `Magnesium chloride` = CHEBI:86345 | a generic name owns the hexahydrate identity |\n| `MgSO .7H O` (17) | synonym on anhydrous `Magnesium sulfate` | a garbled heptahydrate label (noted above) |\n\n## From the second claw#571 review\n\n- **Sodium malate family** (`Sodium malate` 14, `Sodium DL-malate` 11, `Na2-DL-malate` 6, `Na-malate` 6, `Na malate` 4, `Na-DL-malate` 4, `DL-Na-malate` 3, `DL-Sodium malate` 2; 50 occurrences): MIM's `Sodium malate` record sits on CHEBI:91261, disodium **(S)**-malate, while the labels are racemic or stereo-unspecified. The recipes carry CHEBI:91260 (disodium malate).\n- **`H3BO2`** (3): an unreviewed import record grounds this (likely a typo for H3BO3, boric acid) to boronic acid CHEBI:38267.\n\n\n## Update 2026-10-14 (second review of #881)\n\n**Fixed in #881:**\n- `MgSO4 x H2O`, `MgSO4 . H2O` and `MgSO4・H2O` now resolve to the monohydrate `cas:14168-73-1` (#893).\n- `MgSO .7H O` now resolves to the heptahydrate CHEBI:31795 (#899).\n\n**Still open, same class, from the label index on #881's head:**\n\nDamaged-subscript formula labels resolving to the anhydrous form or to a different compound:\n\n| label | `label_index.csv` answer | CultureMech recipe rows |\n|---|---|---:|\n| `CaCl .6H O` | CHEBI:3312, anhydrous CaCl2 | 5 |\n| `ZnCl .6H O` | CHEBI:49976, anhydrous ZnCl2 | 3 |\n| `EDTA.Na .2H O` | CHEBI:64734 (`Na2-EDTA`) | 3 |\n| `CoCl .6H O` | CHEBI:35696, anhydrous CoCl2 | 0 |\n| `FeSO .7H O` | CHEBI:75832, anhydrous FeSO4 | 0 |\n| `LiCl.H O` | CHEBI:48607, anhydrous LiCl | 0 |\n| `NaH PO .2H O` | CHEBI:37585, anhydrous NaH2PO4 | 0 |\n| `ZnSO .7H O` | CHEBI:86463 (`AlK(SO4)2`), a different compound | 0 |\n| `Na SiO .9H O` | CHEBI:86463 (`AlK(SO4)2`), a different compound | 0 |\n\nWater-ratio names resolving to a different hydrate:\n- `cobalt(2+) sulfate--water (1/7)` → CHEBI:53470, anhydrous CoSO4;\n- `Cobalt(II) chloride--water (1/7)` → CHEBI:53503, the hexahydrate.\n\n**Consistency question, not an explicit contradiction:** `Mgso4_X_7_H2o` carries four names, all ChEBI related synonyms of CHEBI:32599:\n- `magnesium sulphate`;\n- `magnesium(II) sulfate`;\n- `sulfuric acid magnesium salt`;\n- `sulphate of magnesia`.\n\nThey resolve to the heptahydrate, while `Magnesium sulfate` resolves to the anhydrous form. Semantic-review finding SEM:f345b845583ac48792ef is open on this.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhvJ8kw","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The approved #669 rollout reviewed `Magnesium_Chloride` against `Mgcl2_X_6_H2o` before considering a merge. Both currently use CHEBI:86345 and hexahydrate chemistry, but the generic history contains both anhydrous CAS 7786-30-3 from name lookup and hexahydrate CAS 7791-18-6 from supplier data, later resolved through the selected target.\n\nThe captured supplier CSV line 275 associates generic aliases with M2670, and [Sigma M2670](https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sial/m2670) explicitly identifies MgCl2·6H2O / 7791-18-6 / 203.30 g/mol. This establishes that product, not every generic recipe occurrence. The inspected current generic-label cohort lacks supplier/CAS/chemistry fields that would settle the whole source scope. ChEBI [6636](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:6636) and [86345](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:86345) both carry the common magnesium chloride name despite distinct forms. Supplier evidence is an inspected web extraction; the historical formulation reference is a lead, not a verified formulation.\n\nDecision for the bounded rollout: SUPPRESS `MgCl2 x 6 H2O` only on `MIM:Magnesium_Chloride / skos:exactMatch / CHEBI:86345`, retaining both YAML records, histories and chemistry. Keep the separate anhydrous `Mgcl2 / CHEBI:6636` owner and row unchanged. Do not merge or infer hydration for all generic sources.\n\nRecommendation: keep the form decision open here. Trace original products/formulations or approve an evidence-backed naming convention before a merge. A later merge must preserve #414 provenance and rejected aliases, choose the surviving owner explicitly and union overlapping memberships rather than adding counts. Native receipts and fresh review remain required. #868 already routes this magnesium identity concern to #811; this comment does not expand the current curation scope.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-01T14:04:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811#issuecomment-6559005843","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkGoqTQ","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Observation at the assigned frozen MIM baseline `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99` (explicit dependency PR #1158), with isolated proposals. This is not a claim about a later main revision.\n\n`data/ingredients/mapped/Alk_So42.yaml` still carries `Na SiO .9H O` and `ZnSO .7H O` as resolving `EXACT_SYNONYM` values on CHEBI:86463 potassium aluminium sulfate. Their sodium/silicon and zinc formula fragments do not denote that aluminium/potassium sulfate identity. The defect does not require guessing a complete intended hydrate formula for either malformed string.\n\nThe independently reviewed isolated `a-proposal-anhydrous-alum` retypes both values to `REJECTED_LABEL`, preserving exact source text and provenance, while adding a separately source-supported explicitly anhydrous alias. Baseline SHA256: `eb7149b3301b2f405c59d0463b04bf6db774703bb3e914d125ffe9086ac717ed`; proposed SHA256: `8b74660fe96d2e9cc2eaeb36ad1e995a6d86f548f817041541959f754f2c60ce`. C166 and the exact proposal bytes were independently reviewed by B in `b/review-a/additional-review-c166.json`.\n\nPreserve `SEM:15761b556078b9a904a8` and `reports/yaml_record_review/Alk_So42.md`. That historical finding also covers CultureMech metadata strings, so rejection of the two foreign fragments does not close the whole finding or approve the entire owner. The older #529 duplicate-synonym issue and #662 confidence-table issue concern different defects and are not substitutes for this existing #811 entry.\n\nFollow-up: guarded integration, withdrawal of inherited support for changed bytes, final full-owner review, and coordinator-controlled synchronization so these values remain provenance-only and do not resolve or enter published `other`. No source ingredient is reassigned to a guessed sodium silicate or zinc sulfate hydrate, no occurrence count is changed, and no downstream rebuild has run in this source-review campaign.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-08T05:41:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811#issuecomment-6717844045","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHXrIg","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"W08-IR-008 independently confirms four remaining resolving phosphate aliases in complete selected payloads at `b90a2fd4681d20e2586481b7b9b1114a78281b94`. The existing generic Potassium phosphate concern applies directly; the malformed formula examples belong to the same bounded owner review.\n\n| Owner | Still-resolving strings | Exact selected payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|\n| K2hpo4.yaml / CHEBI:131527 | `KH2HPO4`, `K2HPO` | `6bd2194c63c815c81750a6e61e6da8d85db6579ebeee15626caf1328bbc645a4` |\n| Kh2po4.yaml / CHEBI:63036 | `KH PO`, `Potassium Phosphate` | `3d0229f92f67f101f4af0975821cbd5ba4e26145c0d8b7f9f5d19ca395708b27` |\n\nThe native synonym function resolves all four. Preserve literal text/history/source credit as REJECTED_LABEL unless a precise primary correction supports a narrower occurrence-bound use. Do not silently transfer source memberships or assume a typo determines a chemical identity. Keep the valid anhydrous-base spelling and prior1215 concentration-alias corrections;1216 molybdate is a separate scope. These are unapplied proposal repairs needing new exact-byte independent review.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-08T07:13:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811#issuecomment-6718614306","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":811,"state":"OPEN","title":"Label-index answers still wrong or missing for CultureMech recipe labels (pin-refresh replay)","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811"}
